=You are building an engineering knowledge graph connecting developers, tasks, repositories, services, APIs, databases, incidents, pull requests, architecture decisions, and documentation.

Below is a snapshot of entities already known to the graph, for reference when matching mentions to existing nodes:

{{ JSON.stringify($json.entities || $json, null, 2) }}

Below are events whose free text may reference other entities that weren't captured by structured fields:

{{ JSON.stringify($('Check for Ambiguous Events').first().json.ambiguousEvents, null, 2) }}

For each event, read its freeText and identify any additional entities it references (by name, ID, or clear description) that its structured fields didn't already capture - for example a task description mentioning a service, a PR body mentioning "fixes INC-1234", a doc page mentioning an API or database, or a description proposing an architectural decision. Match mentions to an existing entity ID from the registry when there's a clear match; otherwise propose a new entity ID using a short slug.

Return a JSON object with EXACTLY this shape:
{
  "extractedLinks": [
    {
      "eventEntityId": "the entityId of the event this link came from, matching input exactly",
      "from": { "type": "developer|task|repository|service|api|database|incident|pull_request|architecture_decision|documentation", "id": "string" },
      "to": { "type": "developer|task|repository|service|api|database|incident|pull_request|architecture_decision|documentation", "id": "string" },
      "relation": "short snake_case relation, e.g. resolves, depends_on, documents, decided_for, causes",
      "confidence": "high" or "low"
    }
  ]
}

Only include links you are reasonably confident about. Return ONLY the JSON. No markdown, no explanation.

